  "findings": [
    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/agent_signal.py:297-303 `_own_entry` calls `_find_item(items, ...)` before any `_entry_signals` validation. `_find_item` (agent_board.py:582-591) calls `item.get(...)` on every item. If the board contains a non-dict item, such as the string \"not an entry\" that the tests append, this raises AttributeError. That error is not a SignalError, so `main` does not catch it and the CLI prints a traceback instead of `agent_signal: ...`. The malformed-entry test covers only `resolve_signal` and `open_signals`, not `raise_signal`.",
      "id": "raise-malformed-entry-traceback",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "`raise` can crash with an unhandled AttributeError on a malformed non-dict board entry. The module's own contract is to report malformed board data as a named SignalError."
    }
  ],
